ema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"user": {"description": "Zero-based active virtual user whose current selected allowed target is captured.", "format": "uint", "minimum": 0, "type": "integer"}}, "required": ["user"], "type": "object"}}, {"name": "routing_displays", "description": "Read the virtual desktop bounds and connected display monitors, including stable monitor interface paths when Windows provides them. This read-only inventory does not load ProtoInput, change displays, or return transient monitor handles. Adapter-name fallbacks are explicitly marked unverified and cannot be persisted as monitor selections.", "inputSchema": {"properties": {}, "type": "object"}, "annotations": {"readOnlyHint": true}}, {"name": "routing_graph", "description": "Inspect, apply or cancel pending replication using stable seat IDs from identities. Version-1 edges have optional options: motion/wheel/horizontal_wheel and five buttons filters, anchored or source_relative position, offset_x/y, click_delay_ms (0-60000), and step_interval_ms (0-1000; temporal pacing, not motion gain). Omitted options preserve anchored immediate legacy behavior. Chains compose per-hop positions and timing; conflicting diamond paths use lexicographic stable-ID paths once per event component. Apply validates endpoints, keyboards, categories, path bounds and cycles before releasing input; active recording/playback and stale expected_revision preserve the graph, queue and held input. Successful Apply releases held input and resumes overflow-suspended replication. Cancel requires the current revision and clears queued copies/replica holds while preserving ordinary/source-program owners, definition and revision; future source events can replicate again. Queue telemetry is automation.replication. Overflow suspends copying until valid Apply; source releases still clean up. All operations stay inside the authorized virtual routing session.", "input